---
// pages/terms.astro — Terms of Service
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { buildTitle, buildCanonical } from '../lib/seo';
import { business, phone } from '../data/client.config';

const title = buildTitle("Terms of Service");
const canonicalUrl = buildCanonical("/terms");
---

<BaseLayout title={title} canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}>
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-20 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 prose prose-green prose-lg">

      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm not-prose">Last updated: April 21, 2026</p>

      <p>
        These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of the website at
        <a href={business.domain}>{business.domain}</a>, operated by Environmental Forest
        Products ("EFP," "we," "us," or "our"). By accessing or using this website, you agree
        to these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use this website.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Use of This Website</h2>
      <p>
        This website is provided for informational purposes and to facilitate contact with
        prospective clients interested in forestry consulting, timber harvesting, land clearing,
        and related services. You agree to use this website only for lawful purposes consistent
        with these Terms and all applicable federal, state, and local laws and regulations.
      </p>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Submit false, misleading, or fraudulent information through any form on this site</li>
        <li>Use the site in any way that could damage, disable, or impair its functionality</li>
        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to any part of this website or its underlying systems</li>
        <li>Use automated means (bots, scrapers, crawlers) to extract or harvest content for commercial purposes</li>
        <li>Transmit spam, unsolicited communications, or malicious code through any form or contact mechanism on this site</li>
        <li>Impersonate any person or entity or misrepresent your affiliation with any person or entity</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Informational Purpose Only — No Professional-Client Relationship</h2>
      <p>
        The content on this website — including service descriptions, guide articles, calculator
        outputs, pricing estimates, regulatory summaries, and any other information — is provided
        for general informational purposes only.
      </p>
      <p>
        Submitting a contact or estimate form, using a calculator tool, or reading content on this
        website does not establish a professional consulting, forestry, or contractual relationship
        between you and Environmental Forest Products. A formal engagement begins only when both
        parties have agreed in writing to a defined scope of work.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Calculator and Estimator Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        This website includes free interactive tools for estimating land clearing costs, timber
        stumpage value, tree removal costs, and 480-a tax savings. These tools are provided as
        general screening aids only and carry the following limitations:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Not a formal appraisal.</strong> Calculator outputs do not constitute a
          professional timber appraisal, certified forestry assessment, or formal quote. Actual
          values depend on site-specific conditions that can only be assessed in person.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Pricing estimates may vary.</strong> Cost ranges are based on typical regional
          pricing in Sullivan, Orange, and Ulster counties, NY, and are updated periodically.
          Actual contractor prices, mill pricing, and regulatory costs change over time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No reliance for financial decisions.</strong> Do not use calculator outputs as
          the sole basis for any financial, legal, tax, or land management decision. Consult a
          licensed forester, tax professional, or attorney for guidance specific to your situation.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>480-a eligibility estimates.</strong> The 480-a savings calculator provides
          illustrative estimates only. Actual eligibility, assessment reductions, and program
          requirements are determined by the New York State Department of Environmental Conservation
          and your local assessor. EFP makes no representations regarding your specific eligibility.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Accuracy of Information</h2>
      <p>
        We make reasonable efforts to keep information on this website accurate and current.
        However, forestry regulations, timber market prices, tax program rules, and service
        availability change. We do not warrant that any content on this site is complete,
        accurate, or current at the time you read it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Regulatory information (such as DEC permit requirements, wetland setbacks, SPDES thresholds,
        or 480-a enrollment criteria) is provided as general background only. Always verify current
        requirements directly with the applicable agency or a licensed professional before proceeding
        with any project.
      </p>

      <h2>5. SMS Communications</h2>
      <p>
        Our contact forms offer optional consent to receive SMS messages from Environmental Forest
        Products. If you opt in, you agree to receive text messages as described at the time of
        consent and as further detailed in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may revoke SMS consent at any time by replying <strong>STOP</strong> to any message.
        Withdrawing consent does not affect your access to our services or any prior agreements.
        Message and data rates may apply. EFP is not responsible for charges from your mobile carrier.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        All content on this website — including text, photographs, graphics, logos, calculator logic,
        and site structure — is the property of Environmental Forest Products or its content
        contributors and is protected by United States copyright law. Unauthorized reproduction,
        redistribution, or commercial use of any content is prohibited without prior written permission.
      </p>
      <p>
        Limited use for personal, non-commercial reference (such as linking to a page or quoting
        a brief passage with attribution) is permitted. If you wish to license content or use our
        materials in any commercial context, contact us at the address below.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>
        This website integrates with the following third-party services, each governed by their
        own terms and privacy policies:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>CRST Web:</strong> CRM and SMS communications platform. Contact data submitted through forms is transmitted to our third-party communications processor.</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare Turnstile:</strong> Bot and spam prevention. Form submissions are verified through Cloudflare's challenge system.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics 4:</strong> Anonymous website traffic analytics.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        EFP is not responsible for the practices, content, or availability of these third-party services.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Environmental Forest Products and its
        principals, employees, and agents shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental,
        consequential, or punitive damages arising from:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your use of, or inability to use, this website or its tools</li>
        <li>Reliance on any information, estimate, or calculator output provided on this site</li>
        <li>Errors, omissions, or inaccuracies in website content</li>
        <li>Unauthorized access to or alteration of your transmissions or data</li>
        <li>Any other matter relating to this website</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This website and all content are provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties
        of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability,
        fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Indemnification</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to indemnify and hold harmless Environmental Forest Products and its principals,
        employees, and agents from any claims, damages, losses, liabilities, and expenses (including
        reasonable attorneys' fees) arising from your use of this website, your violation of these
        Terms, or your violation of any third-party rights.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes to These Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to update these Terms at any time. Changes are effective immediately
        upon posting to this page with an updated date. Your continued use of the website after
        changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms. We encourage you to review
        this page periodically.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Governing Law and Dispute Resolution</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of New York, without regard to its
        conflict of law provisions. Any dispute arising from or relating to these Terms or your
        use of this website shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the state and federal
        courts located in Sullivan County, New York. You consent to personal jurisdiction in those courts.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Severability</h2>
      <p>
        If any provision of these Terms is found to be unenforceable or invalid under applicable
        law, that provision shall be modified to the minimum extent necessary to make it
        enforceable, and the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these Terms may be directed to:</p>
      <address class="not-italic">
        Environmental Forest Products<br />
        Sullivan County, New York<br />
        <a href={`tel:${phone.trackingTel}`}>{business.phone}</a><br />
        <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>
      </address>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
